<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6932" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Căsīnum</span></b> , i,
			n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				town of Latium</i>, <i>east of Aquinium</i>, now
			ruins near <i>S. Germano</i>: its citadel the present
				<i>Monte Casino</i>, <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 7, § 29, p. 86</span></i>
			Bip.; <i><span class="en">id. R. R. 3, 4, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 5,
				9, § 63</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Hence the <i>adjj.</i>,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Căsīnas</span></b> ,
				ātis, <i>of Casinum</i>:
				 ager, <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R.
			136</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Agr. 2, 25, 65</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fundus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Phil. 2, 40, 103</span></i>
			; and <i>absol.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in Casinati or Casinate,</span>”
				<i>in the region of Casinum</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 2, 3, 11</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 2, 103, 106, §
			227</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Căsīnus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i>of Casinum</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nymphae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					12, 527</span></i>
			 dub. (others, Casini Nymphae).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
